{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788999175,"nonce":"yKKMCiXRgzTGnB7sICsdakbFVj0=","title":"Cranelift lowering panics on narrow-integer arithmetic","message":"A function doing arithmetic on an hl.UI8 or hl.UI16 register takes the middle\ntier down:\n\n    panicked at isle_aarch64.rs:3877:\n    internal error: entered unreachable code: no rule matched for term\n    vector_size at src/isa/aarch64/inst.isle line 1649\n    [tier] cranelift lowering panicked for findex=255\n\nThe panic is caught and turned into a tier failure, so hybrid degrades to the\ninterpreter, but under `--mode jit` it becomes an uncaught exception and the\nprogram dies:\n\n    Uncaught exception: JIT tier 0 failed to compile findex 255 (Fun_255)\n\n`vector_size` is asked for a type Cranelift classifies as a vector, so the\nlowering is handing it something other than the plain i8/i16 scalar the\narithmetic needs. Narrow integers are the only shape in the reproducer.\n\nReproducer, one file:\n\n    class T2 {\n      static function main() {\n        var a:hl.UI8 = 250;  var b:hl.UI8 = a + 1;\n        Sys.println(\"250+1  = \" + (b : Int));\n        var c:hl.UI8 = 255;  var d:hl.UI8 = c + 1;\n        Sys.println(\"255+1  = \" + (d : Int));\n        var e:hl.UI8 = 200;  var f:hl.UI8 = e * 2;\n        Sys.println(\"200*2  = \" + (f : Int));\n        var g:hl.UI16 = 65535; var h:hl.UI16 = g + 1;\n        Sys.println(\"65535+1= \" + (h : Int));\n      }\n    }\n\n    haxe -hl t2.hl -main T2 -cp .\n    ash --mode jit t2.hl          # panics\n    ash --build t2bin t2.hl       # fine, LLVM lowers it\n\nNothing in the test corpus or the Haxe 4.3.6 conformance tree has a UI8/UI16\narithmetic destination, which is why no suite catches it.","files":null}]}